{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AdjacencyList","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The vertex set is any set of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"text":" values. The edge set is a set of ordered pairs of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices: self-loops are allowed, parallel edges are not.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Vertices are kept in dense slots, with a dictionary from vertex to slot. While the vertices are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<n","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in order, each is its own slot and there is no dictionary. Edges are kept in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an array, so an edge’s position in ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<edgeCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A weight or other","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value per edge or vertex lives in a map attached to the graph (","type":"text"},{"code":"addEdgeMap(default:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"PropertyGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), which every mutation keeps in step.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each slot has a row of the slots of its out-neighbors, a parallel row of those edges’"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"positions, and a row of its in-neighbors. The rows of each kind share one array, so the graph"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"makes an amortized constant number of allocations however many vertices it has, and copying it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"copies a constant number of buffers. A hash table from slot pair to position answers"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contains(edge:)"},{"type":"text","text":" in O(1) expected. A graph built in bulk from sorted edges (a condensation, a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"line graph, a named graph) builds that table in O(m) on its first lookup or mutation, so a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"result that is only traversed never pays for it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Removing an edge is O(1). The last edge moves into its position, and the last entry of each row","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"into the hole. Removing a vertex costs O(degree) and moves the last slot into its place. Vertex","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order, edge order and edge positions are therefore unspecified and may change after a removal.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Attached maps move their values with them, and each insertion or removal appends or moves one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value per map.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule"]]},"abstract":[{"text":